  "title": "[Evidence] DIR-064: DIR-064: Eliminate PDF Blank Page & Skip-Link Bleed, Fix Footer Overlap (Certification Card Geometry), and Centralized Cross-Platform Export Pipeline",
  "sender": "STAFF_DEVELOPER",
  "directiveId": "DIR-064",
  "summary": "DIR-064 COMPLETE, all three P0 defects fixed at their confirmed root causes. (A) SKIP-LINK / BLANK PDF PAGE 1: root cause was cuba-print.css rule 3 forcing '*' { position: static !important } under @media print, which neutralised the skip-link's off-screen top:-100px so it printed as a black banner at the top of page 1 and pushed the resume to page 2. Fixed at four layers: index.html critical CSS now has an additive @media print { .skip-link { display:none !important } } while KEEPING the screen rule (top:-100px + :focus top:0.75rem), so the fouc-prevention and p1-gap accessibility contracts stay green; src/styles/cuba-print.css adds .skip-link to the print chrome-hiding group; Exporter.jsx hides and restores the skip-link around the export surface; backend/index.js removes it from the live DOM via page.evaluate BEFORE page.pdf() and stamps data-print-export. (B) CERT CARDS CLIPPING THE FOOTER: smartPartitioner.js charged a 2-column cert row only 52px while the real card is 74-85px, so ~30px per row was unaccounted and the tail clipped at the page-body edge. Replaced with a title/meta/density-aware estimator CERT_ROW_MIN_PX 76 / CERT_ROW_MAX_PX 88 (certRowHeightFor), recalibrated the sidebar cert height off the same estimator, and subtracted FOOTER_SAFETY_CLEARANCE 22 from P1_CAPACITY/PN_CAPACITY; smartEngine.css adds a 14px bottom buffer on .smart-page-body plus break-inside:avoid on .smart-cert-item. (C) CENTRALIZED CROSS-PLATFORM DOWNLOADER: created src/utils/exportDownloader.js as the single source for PDF+DOCX - reuses the unit-tested %PDF-/PK magic-byte validators, sanitizes filenames against traversal, attaches a Firebase Bearer token that is never logged, exposes downloadResumePdf/downloadResumeDocx, and is pure JS with zero OS process spawning (no winget/PowerShell/platform paths). All six consumer portals (BuildResume, BoardFilling, DashboardHomepage, PublicResume, JobApplicationsModal, EnterpriseResumePdfModal) now import from it and no longer import pdfDownload/docxDownload directly. EVIDENCE: new tests/dir064-pdf-print-export-pipeline.test.mjs 12/12 (incl. FUNCTIONAL assertions that a cert row reserves >=76px from the real partitioner and that the %PDF- validator rejects a JSON error body); export-client + docx-client-journey + dir048-shell-and-controls 19/19 (contract tests updated to the new single-source architecture, intent preserved); fouc-prevention + dir064-wake-supersede + p1-gap 17/17; backend export/docx pipeline 38/38; dir063 6/6; product slice 110/110 (incl. 'no resume item is dropped by the partitioner' and all 55 templates server-rendering). GATES: lint 0 errors (253 pre-existing warnings); security:static 67/67; build 'built in 2.74s' (wall 3.84s, under the 4.0s budget). FROZEN BASELINE: git diff for src/cv-templates is 0 lines. Servers untouched (XAMPP-only); the one foreground vite the cross-app browser suite spawned was terminated. HONEST LIMITS: the PDF page-1/skip-link and footer-overlap fixes are verified by static + functional unit contracts and a real-Chromium pipeline suite, but not by a live end-to-end PDF render in this environment (no live authenticated export host was available); the cert estimator is calibrated to the measured 74-85px card and clamps at 88px, so a pathological 4+ line title could still exceed it (the 14px CSS buffer and break-inside:avoid are the backstop)."
}